      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yepp. Me and several of my friends are using the beta-provided nameplate and icon frame, but not the effects. Please, emphasize the profile, not the effect.\n\nFor moderation, opening someone's profile and having to see this every time is straining on the eyes. We should have an option to disable the profile animation entirely if we want to. Discord still gets this wrong by having you turn off every animation in the client to turn off profile effects. If you're going to copy their style, please consider being even better than theirs.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-07-23T14:42:03.476Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Profile decorations seem overly large and bleed into the contents of the container.\n\nRefer to the image. Red line for where the current bleed stops, blue line as an example of a smaller bleed to not disrupt contents.\n\nDiscord solves this by either having:\n\n1. Decorations fade out after initial decoration animation is finished.\n\n2. Persistent decoration with thinner bleed or decoration on the outside instead.\n\nHope to see the new decorations being less disruptive to text and contents overall.",
